# House Access — deny by default.
#
# This repository root sits inside a House Party installation. A mistake here
# does not merely add clutter, it publishes game files, another author's
# decompiled code, or a compiled binary. So nothing is tracked unless it is
# named below, and new entries are added one deliberate line at a time.
#
# Never use `git add -f` in this repository. If a file needs to ship, admit it
# here where the decision is visible in the history.

# 1. Ignore every top-level entry, then re-admit only what we publish.
/*

!/.gitignore
!/.gitattributes
!/.githooks/
!/README.md
!/CHANGELOG.md
!/CONTRIBUTING.md
!/CRASH-FIX-GUIDE.md
!/docs/
!/port/
!/fix-bepinex-config.bat

# Explicitly ignore NOTICE.md and release bundles
/NOTICE.md
/release/

# 2. Build output, wherever it appears, including inside an admitted folder.
bin/
obj/
*.cache
*.Up2Date
*.AssemblyInfo.cs
*.GeneratedMSBuildEditorConfig.editorconfig

# 3. Binaries. The mod's own DLL is a release download, never a commit.
*.dll
*.pdb
*.exe
*.so
*.dylib
*.lib
*.zip
*.7z
*.rar
*.bin
*.db
*.log

# 4. Game-derived and third-party-derived material. Redundant against rule 1 on
#    purpose: these are the paths that must stay unreachable even if rule 1 is
#    ever loosened.
BepInEx/
MelonLoader/
Mods/

# 5. Local editor and OS noise.
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo
*.swp
*~
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
